  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If it could be possible to have an option to attach the view port empty (I forgot the exact name) but the part of the avatar descriptor where you set the eye height to an empty. This way we could move out view port in different parts of the avatar or have different toggled locations to see kinda like a camera system where you out down a camera with a world constraint and you can toggle your eyes to constraint back to that camera so you can see out of it.\n\nThis would allow for avatars to have different meshes and heights if they use the same armature or rotation constraints. Since I do a lot of rp stuff and swapping models kinda ruins immersion so I'd just like a way to say transform into a massive creature seamlessly without having to swap avatars due to height differences.",
